## SUPERSEDED — DO NOT MERGE

While this control-plane repair was being source-reviewed, merged #1450 and #1459 advanced `main` with the same required fixes plus stronger custody:
- `/usr/bin/git` exact-head observation;
- isolated `/usr/bin/python3 -I` retained-evidence verification;
- a closed Git environment (`GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM`, null global config, no replace objects) for the post-build checkout proof;
- retained built `NembraCaptureFieldRecipe` bound to the external record plus a detached-recipe self-red-team;
- `if-no-files-found: error` for retained artifacts;
- a final live PR/head revalidation after artifact retention.

Fresh inspection of `main@4a98cd96e39350fda77dbf08d2eed038d59ed462` confirms those bytes are deployed. This branch therefore has no unique product or acceptance value and is closed rather than creating duplicate control-plane lineage.

No app/package/BLE/physical bytes were changed here. **PHYSICAL EXPERIMENT ONE REMAINS NO-GO / DO NOT RUN.**

## Root cause
The previous Pages gate assumed that merging the reviewed data PR with the workflow `GITHUB_TOKEN` would trigger the normal `push` Pages workflow. GitHub intentionally suppresses most recursive workflow runs caused by `GITHUB_TOKEN`; `workflow_dispatch` is the supported exception.

## Production fix
- add optional `target_sha` to `deploy-pages.yml` manual dispatch;
- checkout that exact SHA in both impact and deployment jobs;
- write `deployment.json.commit_sha` from the pinned release SHA and verify the live origin against the same SHA;
- after reviewed-data merge, fail closed if `main` has already moved away from that merge SHA;
- dispatch `deploy-pages.yml` via the Actions REST endpoint with `target_sha=<reviewed merge SHA>`;
- consume the returned `workflow_run_id`, watch that exact run, and require success before #606 can become current/closed;
- regression-test both orchestration and Pages release identity.

This keeps the full production-ready acceptance chain transactional without using a PAT, adding a fallback path, or weakening any model/data/replay/session/publication gate.

Refs #606
